{"content":[{"c":["DESTROYER, The"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Divine agent sent to carry out a sentence of destruction. The destroyer killed Egypt’s firstborn, culminating the plagues and releasing the Hebrews from slavery (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.12.23","r":"Exod.12.23","rawR":"Exod.12.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.12.23","value":"Exod.12.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 12:23"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.11.28","r":"Heb.11.28","rawR":"Heb.11.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.11.28","value":"Heb.11.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 11:28"},"). The apostle Paul used the term for God’s judgment on the rebellious Israelites in the wilderness (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.10.10","r":"1Cor.10.10","rawR":"1Cor.10.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.10.10","value":"1Cor.10.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 10:10"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Num.16.44-50","r":"Num.16.44-50","rawR":"Num.16.44-50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.16.44-50","value":"Num.16.44-50"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 16:44-50"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. In plural form, “destroyers” implies destruction carried out by a group of agents, whether angelic or human (",{"href":"?bref=Job.33.22","r":"Job.33.22","rawR":"Job.33.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.33.22","value":"Job.33.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 33:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.22.7","r":"Jer.22.7","rawR":"Jer.22.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.22.7","value":"Jer.22.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 22:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. In a broader sense, any agent of destruction (",{"href":"?bref=Job.15.21","r":"Job.15.21","rawR":"Job.15.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.15.21","value":"Job.15.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 15:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.4.7","r":"Jer.4.7","rawR":"Jer.4.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.4.7","value":"Jer.4.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 4:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Samson was called a destroyer by his Philistine captors (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.16.24","r":"Judg.16.24","rawR":"Judg.16.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.16.24","value":"Judg.16.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 16:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Destroyerthe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 12:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.12.23","rawQueryValue":"Exod.12.23","sourceRefExact":"Exod.12.23"},{"anchorText":"Heb 11:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Heb.11.28","rawQueryValue":"Heb.11.28","sourceRefExact":"Heb.11.28"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 10:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.10.10","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.10.10","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.10.10"},{"anchorText":"Nm 16:44-50","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.16.44-50","rawQueryValue":"Num.16.44-50","sourceRefExact":"Num.16.44-50"},{"anchorText":"Jb 33:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.33.22","rawQueryValue":"Job.33.22","sourceRefExact":"Job.33.22"},{"anchorText":"Jer 22:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.22.7","rawQueryValue":"Jer.22.7","sourceRefExact":"Jer.22.7"},{"anchorText":"Jb 15:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.15.21","rawQueryValue":"Job.15.21","sourceRefExact":"Job.15.21"},{"anchorText":"Jer 4:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.4.7","rawQueryValue":"Jer.4.7","sourceRefExact":"Jer.4.7"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 16:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.16.24","rawQueryValue":"Judg.16.24","sourceRefExact":"Judg.16.24"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5f794f6c0555067ccb9c51740cbe41f16009ebf8370bc74fb2be302cc7a8fa56","sourceItemName":"Destroyerthe","sourceItemOrd